What this licence covers
------------------------

The licence above covers Calimocho's own work: the Wine patches in
patches/, the build and packaging scripts, the native-GS loader helper
(tools/native_gs_localtime.c) and the documentation.

Engine releases also contain software from other projects. Each keeps
its own licence. The full licence texts ship in every release under
licenses/, and SOURCE.md in every release says where to get the
corresponding source.


Components under open-source licences
-------------------------------------

| Component | Upstream | Licence |
|---|---|---|
| Wine 11.20 | https://www.winehq.org/ | LGPL-2.1-or-later |
| Libraries vendored in Wine's libs/ (vkd3d, FAudio, mpg123, lcms2, libpng, libjpeg, libtiff, libxml2, libxslt, zlib, musl, capstone, ...) | Wine source tree | Their own licences, kept in the Wine source tree; vkd3d is LGPL-2.1-or-later |
| D3DMetal integration patch, derived from CodeWeavers' CrossOver 26.3.0 source | https://www.codeweavers.com/crossover/source | LGPL-2.1-or-later |
| FreeType 2.13.3 | https://freetype.org/ | FTL or GPL-2.0; Calimocho distributes it under the FTL (licenses/freetype/ELECTED.txt) |
| GnuTLS 3.8.13 | https://www.gnutls.org/ | LGPL-2.1-or-later (library) |
| libtasn1 4.21.0 | https://www.gnu.org/software/libtasn1/ | LGPL-2.1-or-later (library) |
| nettle 4.0 | https://www.lysator.liu.se/~nisse/nettle/ | LGPL-3.0-or-later or GPL-2.0-or-later |
| GMP 6.3.0 | https://gmplib.org/ | LGPL-3.0-or-later or GPL-2.0-or-later |
| MoltenVK 1.4.2, with SPIRV-Cross, SPIRV-Tools, SPIRV-Headers, Vulkan-Headers, Vulkan-Tools, cereal and Volk | https://github.com/KhronosGroup/MoltenVK | Apache-2.0; the components keep their own licences |

Highball tsshim, used only by the Forza Horizon 6 profile:

| Component | Upstream | Licence |
|---|---|---|
| d3d12 tsshim (lib/wine/x86_64-windows/d3d12_tsshim.dll), built from commit 1512223fff145eae3b4c9fb588edf86758bc756b | https://github.com/gauthierpiarrette/highball | GPL-3.0 |

Calimocho's only change to the tsshim is its export name in d3d12.def,
d3d12_tsshim.dll instead of d3d12.dll. The shim is inactive unless the
Forza Horizon 6 profile copies it into that game's prefix. Its source
and licence ship in licenses/highball-tsshim/ and in the source
tarball.

These licences do not restrict commercial use. They do require that
you pass on the licence texts and make the corresponding source
available when you redistribute the binaries.

Portions of this software are copyright © 1996-2024 The FreeType
Project (www.freetype.org).  All rights reserved.


Apple D3DMetal (not covered by the LGPL)
----------------------------------------

Apple's D3DMetal, from the Game Porting Toolkit, is closed source and
has a restrictive licence. Engine releases include these Apple files,
unmodified:

- D3DMetal.framework
- libd3dshared.dylib
- the Direct3D PE modules under lib/wine/x86_64-windows that come from
  the Game Porting Toolkit

D3DMetal contains xxHash (https://github.com/Cyan4973/xxHash),
BSD-2-Clause. Its licence text ships in licenses/xxhash/LICENSE.

They are distributed under the Apple Game Porting Toolkit licence,
reproduced in THIRDPARTY/Apple-GPTK/License.rtf and in
licenses/apple-gptk/ in every release. In that licence:

- Section 2A(iii) allows you to "distribute the Apple Software solely
  for non-commercial purposes and in accordance with this Agreement,
  including Section 2C".
- Section 2A requires that you "reproduce on each copy of the Apple
  Software or portion thereof, all copyright or other proprietary
  notices contained on the original".
- Section 2C says "the Framework in its entirety or any part of the
  Redistributables may be distributed separately from the Apple
  Software" and "all distribution of the Apple Software, including the
  Framework in its entirety and any individual Redistributables, are
  subject to the non-commercial restriction in Section 2(A)(iii)".
- Section 2C also says "You may not rent, lease, lend, host, sell, or
  sublicense (except as expressly set forth in Section 2A) the Apple
  Software or any services, in whole or in part". It bars use for
  service bureau, time-sharing or similar services, and bars use on
  non-Apple-branded devices.
- Section 2D forbids you to "decompile, reverse engineer, disassemble,
  attempt to derive the source code of, decrypt, modify, or create
  derivative works of the Apple Software".

What this means:

- Calimocho is distributed free of charge, for non-commercial use.
- A release that contains the Apple files may only be redistributed
  non-commercially, unmodified, and with Apple's notices intact.
- If you want to distribute Calimocho commercially, remove the Apple
  files. Everything that remains is under the open-source licences
  above.
- The non-commercial condition comes from Apple's licence and applies
  only to the Apple files. It is not an additional restriction on the
  LGPL-licensed components.

The Calimocho authors are not lawyers, and nothing here is legal
advice. For a binding interpretation, read Apple's licence in full.

See also NOTICE (credits) and TRADEMARKS.md.
